<title>UK: TABLE TENNIS-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TABLE TENNIS-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MANCHESTER, England 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the penultimate day of the world table tennis championships on Sunday (prefix numbers denote seeding):</p>
<p>Mixed doubles semifinals</p>
<p>1-Kong Linghui/Deng Yaping (China) beat 9/16-Chiang Peng-lung/Chen Jing (Taiwan) 21-16 21-16 15-21 21-7</p>
<p>2-Liu Guoliang/Wu Na (China) beat Wang Liqin/Wang Nan (China) 20-22 21-15 21-17 21-9  </p>
<p>Men's doubles quarter-finals</p>
<p>5/8-Koji Matsushita/Hiroshi Shibutani (Japan) beat 3/4-Wang</p>
<p>Tao/Ma Lin (China) 21-15 21-19 21-15</p>
<p>2-Jan-Ove Waldner/Jorgen Persson (Sweden) beat 9/16-Werner</p>
<p>Schlager/Karl Jindrak (Austria) 19-21 21-19 27-25 21-16</p>
<p>Men's doubles quarter-finals</p>
<p>1-Kong Linghui/Liu Guoliang (China) beat 5/8-Vladimir Samsonov</p>
<p>(Belarus)/Joerg Rosskopf (Germany) 17-21 21-12 21-13 21-10</p>
<p>Women's doubles quarter-finals</p>
<p>1-Deng Yaping/Yang Ying (China) beat 9/16-Chen Jing/Chen</p>
<p>Chiu-tan (Taiwan) 21-16 21-7 21-10</p>
<p>Women's doubles quarter-finals</p>
<p>3/4-Qiao Yungping (China)/Chai Po Wa (Hong Kong) beat 5/8-Wang</p>
<p>Chen/Wu Na (China) 21-10 21-12 21-11</p>
<p>Wang Hui/Cheng Hongxia (China) beat Otilia Badescu/Emilia Ciosu</p>
<p>(Romania) 21-17 21-9 21-16</p>
<p>Men's doubles quarter-finals</p>
<p>5/8-Jean-Philippe Gatien/Damien Eloi (France) beat 3/4-Yan</p>
<p>Sen/Wang Liqin (China) 21-10 21-10 12-21 22-20</p>
<p>(Ends men's quarter-finals)</p>
<p>Semifinals:</p>
<p>1-Kong Linghui/Liu Guoliang (China) v 5/8-Gatien/Eloi </p>
<p>5/8-Koji Matsushita/Hiroshi Shibutani (Japan) v 2-Jan-Ove</p>
<p>Waldner/Jorgen Persson (Sweden)</p>
<p>Women's doubles quarter-finals</p>
<p>3/4-Li Ju/Wang Nan (China) beat Ai Sakata/Yuki Takakusa (Japan)</p>
<p>21-9 21-15 21-15</p>
<p>(Ends women's quarter-finals)</p>
<p>Semifinals: </p>
<p>1-Deng Yaping/Yang Ying (China) v 3/4-Qiao Yunping (China)/Chai</p>
<p>Po Wa (Hong Kong)</p>
<p>3/4-Li Ju/Wang Nan (China) v 5/8-Wang Hui/Cheng Hongxia (China)</p>
<p>Mixed doubles final</p>
<p>2-Liu Guoliang/Wu Na (China) beat 1-Kong Linghui/Deng Yaping</p>
<p>(China) 21-12 22-20 19-21 21-11</p>
<p>Women's singles quarter-final</p>
<p>5/8-Wang Nan (China) beat Cheng Hongxia (China) 21-18 22-20</p>
<p>18-21 21-9</p>
<p>Men's singles quarter-final</p>
<p>2-Jan-Ove Waldner (Sweden) beat 9/16-Jean-Philippe Gatien</p>
<p>(France) 21-7 22-20 21-14</p>
<p>Men's singles quarter-finals</p>
<p>Yan Sen (China) beat He Zhi Wen (Spain) 21-19 19-21 21-13 21-19</p>
<p>Women's singles quarter-finals</p>
<p>9/16-Wu Na (China) beat 9/16-Nicole Struse (Germany) 21-16</p>
<p>21-13 21-18</p>
<p>Men's singles quarter-finals</p>
<p>1-Kong Linghui (China) beat 9/16-Ma Wenge (China) 16-21 22-20</p>
<p>14-21 21-15 21-12</p>
<p>Men's singles quarter-finals</p>
<p>3/4-Vladimir Samsonov (Belarus) beat 5/8-Ding Song (China)</p>
<p>21-13 21-9 21-10</p>
<p>Semifinals: </p>
<p>1-Kong Linghui (China) v Samsonov</p>
<p>Yan Sen (China) v 2-Jan-Ove Waldner (Sweden)</p>
</text>
